Subject: CPMS I03 Semantic Residual and Conformance Constraint Ledger

@ [ledger_uuid] be270e03-b2e0-436f-a987-2327c89a074f

& [IdentityConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C01 consume only the six fixed I02 artifacts after exact path length digest profile dialect id root and source-lineage verification
  + I03-C02 each root kind maps to exactly one input-deserialize or output-serialize document and actual Rust type
  + I03-C03 residual case rule and diagnostic identities are stable nonempty bounded SemanticId values
  + I03-C04 intended-use root identity is never merged by equal raw schema or equal Rust type

& [IngressConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C05 supplied input is bounded exact UTF-8 bytes and no lossy string conversion occurs
  + I03-C06 one recursive visitor rejects duplicate member names at every depth before releasing a Value
  + I03-C07 malformed lexical input invalid UTF-8 trailing non-whitespace data depth exhaustion and structural counter exhaustion fail atomically
  + I03-C08 parser accounting covers bytes depth object members array items scalar values and maximum member-name bytes
  + I03-C09 typed serde consumes the original exact bytes independently and requires end-of-input

& [ValidatorConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C10 validator is exact-pinned and uses Draft 2020-12 explicitly rather than auto-detected drift
  + I03-C11 default features are disabled and no HTTP filesystem async or custom external retriever exists
  + I03-C12 schema meta-validation local-reference rescan and expected digest verification precede validator construction
  + I03-C13 every non-fragment or unresolved reference refuses before instance validation
  + I03-C14 format validation policy is explicit and stable; no ambient format behavior is inferred
  + I03-C15 engine-native diagnostics are normalized into sorted bounded records and native display text is non-authoritative context only

& [ResidualConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C16 every document residual id resolves exactly once and every registry record names at least one exact root
  + I03-C17 every non-syntactic acceptance gate observed on the five public operation roots is assigned a registry family
  + I03-C18 enforced records name exact crate module function stage condition and proof
  + I03-C19 unimplemented and partial records cannot produce semantic pass
  + I03-C20 residual registry digest covers profile records ordering and CPMS-I02 bundle digest
  + I03-C21 no residual is encoded as a private JSON Schema keyword

& [CorpusConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C22 cases are unique lexically ordered root-qualified and immutable after activation
  + I03-C23 every case binds exact supplied bytes expected ingress schema serde and optional semantic outcomes
  + I03-C24 every common syntax claim has positive and negative witness coverage when constructible
  + I03-C25 minimum maximum below at above missing null unknown wrong type tag enum duplicate cardinality and recursive-depth families are accounted present not-applicable or deferred with reason
  + I03-C26 duplicate-key cases stop after ingress refusal for governing disposition while raw serde observation remains informational
  + I03-C27 output serialization roots are checked by serializing actual typed fixtures then schema-validating the resulting faithful value; arbitrary untrusted bytes do not claim Rust output constructibility
  + I03-C28 corpus profile caps 4096 cases and 67108864 aggregate supplied bytes

& [ComparisonConstraints] are closed
  + I03-C29 agreement is evaluated only where both readers are applicable and a CommonSyntaxClaim exists
  + I03-C30 skipped not-applicable exhausted panic or internal fault never counts as accepted rejected or agreement
  + I03-C31 every disagreement preserves case reader expected actual rule schema path and bounded diagnostics
  + I03-C32 repeat execution over identical bundle registry corpus engine and code must be byte-equivalent after normalized sorting
  + I03-C33 engine panic or nondeterministic normalized result is a release-blocking internal fault

& [ThreeGateConstraints] are constitutional
  + I03-C34 byte schema and serde syntax observations do not imply semantic validity
  + I03-C35 semantic evaluation does not imply authority admission
  + I03-C36 no syntax or semantic result claims truth safety permission effectlessness production fitness or compatibility of changed schemas

& [ResourceConstraints] are finite before activation
  + I03-C37 per supplied instance maximum bytes is 16777216
  + I03-C38 maximum instance structural depth is 128 including root container
  + I03-C39 maximum aggregate object members is 65536
  + I03-C40 maximum aggregate array items is 65536
  + I03-C41 maximum aggregate scalar values is 131072
  + I03-C42 maximum member-name bytes is 4096
  + I03-C43 maximum normalized findings per case is 256
  + I03-C44 maximum normalized diagnostic text is 1024 characters per finding
  + I03-C45 inherited document bundle schema and residual ceilings remain active

& [ProcessConstraints] preserve SJS
  + I03-C46 source canonical exploded requirements activation solution review and proof remain distinct records
  + I03-C47 formation changes no Cargo Rust JSON golden or runtime file
  + I03-C48 activation requires exact dependency resolution offline cache audit no-resolution compile proof and a closed source-touch lock

& [ForbiddenShortcuts] are explicit
  + pre-parsing to Value before duplicate inspection
  + interpreting last-key-wins as duplicate-free conformance
  + enabling validator defaults or external reference retrieval
  + using engine display strings as stable protocol identity
  + counting both-skipped or both-faulted as agreement
  + declaring a complete residual registry from RMS-R01 through RMS-R06 alone
  + running semantic operations on incoherent partial fixtures
  + claiming exhaustive schema-serde equivalence from a finite corpus
  + adding provider model service persistence network effect compatibility production or hardware behavior
